# ---------------------------------------- W4: a signal refused otherwise

[break] a-refused-signal-is-gone
rule: Only ESRCH says a process /proc does not show is gone: any other refusal of a signal of nothing (a security module's EACCES) leaves it not known.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session/channel.rs
in: whose
find: Err(_) => Whose::NotKnown
replace: Err(_) => Whose::Gone
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::channel::tests::whose_a_process_is_is_told_by_a_signal_of_nothing

[break] a-process-whose-owner-is-not-known-ends-the-line
rule: A process of the line that /proc does not show, whose owner a signal of nothing cannot tell, is not known, and refuses.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
in: hidden
find: Whose::NotKnown => Seen::Failed
replace: Whose::NotKnown => Seen::Unseen
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::sys::tests::a_process_proc_does_not_show_is_told_by_whose_it_is

# ------------------------------------- W5: rules no test held before

[break] another-users-process-is-not-known
rule: A process /proc does not show that a signal of nothing may not be sent to (EPERM) is another user's, and ends the line elsewhere.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session/channel.rs
in: whose
find: Err(libc::EPERM) => Whose::Others,
replace: Err(libc::EPERM) => Whose::NotKnown,
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::channel::tests::whose_a_process_is_is_told_by_a_signal_of_nothing

[break] a-refused-stat-is-gone
rule: A process whose stat cannot be read (ENOENT, EACCES) is asked whose it is: one of this user's that is there is not known, and refuses.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
in: seen
find: return hidden(own, pid);
replace: return Seen::Unseen;
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::sys::tests::a_live_process_of_this_user_whose_stat_is_refused_is_not_known

[break] a-word-of-another-user-counts
rule: A word is held only where the process that made it, as the kernel gives it (SO_PEERCRED), is of this process's user.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session/channel.rs
in: read_one
find: asked != 0 || peer.uid != uid
replace: asked != 0
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::channel::tests::a_word_counts_only_where_its_maker_is_of_this_user
